CABINET — MODELLING PLAN (surface draft; to be refined)
Metres unless stated; values in braces are this object's parameters. Z up, floor at Z 0. Hosted on a point: origin at the placement point on the floor.

WHAT IT IS
contemporary base cabinet, matte laminate doors, stone worktop — styled to the kitchen pick: greige lacquer and light-oak joinery, brass hardware.

GEOMETRY
Model the object described above as clean, closed meshes with real thickness and small bevels on exposed edges (about 2 mm) so highlights catch. Drive every dimension from these parameters:
- Width: {width}
- Depth: {depth}
- Height: {height}
- Panel thickness: {panelThk}
- Worktop: {worktop}
- Worktop thickness: {worktopThk}
- Worktop overhang: {worktopOver}
- Doors: {doors}
- Drawers above doors: {drawers}
- Drawer front height: {drawerHeight}
- Plinth height: {plinthHeight}
- Internal shelves: {shelves}
- Handles: {handles}
- Rotation (deg): {rotation}
- Anchor Direction: {anchorDir} (one of: Top-Left / Top-Center / Top-Right / Left-Center / Center / Right-Center / Bottom-Left / Bottom-Center / Bottom-Right)
- Margin from host: {margin}
- Flip side: {flipSide}
Keep the proportions of a well-made real product; add the secondary detail a close-up render needs (joints, reveals, fixings) but no hidden interior geometry.

MATERIALS
Greige matt lacquer fronts, light-oak veneer, brushed-brass handles; stone worktop in soft white. Colours come from the colour params below (set from the pick's palette).
- Base colour: {baseColor}
- Roughness: {roughness}
Principled BSDF per visible part, using the colour and roughness above for the main surface; secondary parts in a neutral complementary finish. Use Object / box-projected texture coordinates (no UVs needed). Add a subtle noise bump (strength ~0.03) so surfaces are not perfectly flat.

LIGHTS
None. This object does not emit light.

